{
  "schema": "ffw.p06.durable_abi.v1",
  "provenance": "Written by hand. The numbers are the values in the Linux headers at v2.6.14, v2.6.23, v2.6.33 and v2.6.35 (asm-generic and the asm-mips / asm-powerpc fcntl.h and errno.h; the files and their sha256 are under 'witnesses') and in the libc crate's musl b32 MIPS and PowerPC files (0.2.191). The sums in 'open_request' are typed as literals; the first three were added up by hand, the rest by tests/p06/test_durable.py's independent model and then compared. Nothing in this file was produced by the Rust under test; tests/p06/test_durable.py re-derives every decoded answer and holds every number to the libc files. The facts about kernel behavior (O_CLOEXEC ignored before 2.6.23, fsync reporting an error once, EXDEV on a cross-mount rename, pread64 taking six argument slots) are read from the sources under 'witnesses', not observed on a running kernel.",
